EXAMPLE FILE — NOT LIVE. Rename to `assetlinks.json` and deploy to
https://proaudiotrainingacademy.com/.well-known/ . One value is still MISSING
and is marked below; do not deploy with the placeholder in place.

VERIFIED VALUES (2026-09-05)
  Android package   com.cbcreativeservices.apestudio   (app.json android.package)
  Intent filters    ALREADY IN THE SHIPPED BUILD. Confirmed by reading the
                    binary AndroidManifest.xml out of the 2026-09-05 dev APK
                    (build fb10c2f2, versionCode 10): both hosts, autoVerify,
                    VIEW + BROWSABLE + DEFAULT, and the /get /tools /learn /labs
                    /glossary /awards /directory /careers prefixes are present.
                    So Android app links start working the moment this file is
                    live and a build from 2026-09-05 or later is installed.

MISSING VALUE — the SHA-256 certificate fingerprint
  This must be the fingerprint of the certificate that signs the app AS
  INSTALLED ON USERS' DEVICES. Getting this wrong is the single most common
  reason app links silently fail to verify.

  - If Play App Signing is enabled (it is, for any app distributed through
    Play), the correct fingerprint is the PLAY APP SIGNING key, which you read
    from Play Console → your app → Test and release → Setup → App signing.
    It is NOT your upload key.
  - The EAS build credential (`eas credentials -p android`) is the UPLOAD key.
    Useful for verifying internal-distribution APKs like the current dev
    builds, but wrong for anything installed from Play.
  - You may legitimately list BOTH: the Play app-signing fingerprint so Play
    installs verify, and the upload/dev fingerprint so internally distributed
    builds verify too. Both entries below are the same shape; add or remove as
    needed and keep a comment in your deployment notes saying which is which.

  The app is not on Play yet, so only the second is obtainable today:
      eas credentials -p android      → Keystore → SHA-256 Fingerprint

DEPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS
  - HTTPS, Content-Type: application/json, no redirect, no authentication.
  - The gate (web/lib/gate.ts GATE_ENABLED) must not cover /.well-known/*.
  - Fingerprints are UPPERCASE hex, colon-separated.

[
  {
    "relation": ["delegate_permission/common.handle_all_urls"],
    "target": {
      "namespace": "android_app",
      "package_name": "com.cbcreativeservices.apestudio",
      "sha256_cert_fingerprints": [
        "REPLACE_WITH_PLAY_APP_SIGNING_SHA256_FROM_PLAY_CONSOLE",
        "REPLACE_WITH_EAS_UPLOAD_SHA256_FROM_eas_credentials_-p_android"
      ]
    }
  }
]

AFTER DEPLOYING, verify:
  curl -s https://proaudiotrainingacademy.com/.well-known/assetlinks.json | jq .
  Google's tester:
    https://digitalassetlinks.googleapis.com/v1/statements:list?source.web.site=https://proaudiotrainingacademy.com&relation=delegate_permission/common.handle_all_urls
  On device (verification runs at install time, so reinstall after deploying):
    adb shell pm get-app-links com.cbcreativeservices.apestudio
        expect: proaudiotrainingacademy.com  verified
    adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW \
        -d "https://proaudiotrainingacademy.com/glossary/phantom-power"
  Play Console also reports this under Grow → Deep links once the app is uploaded.
